{
  "dom_id": "step-e21517",
  "name": "Example: Applying Percentage Increases Greater Than 100%",
  "problem": "A number $x$ is $150\\%$ greater than $20.$ Find the value of $x.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find a number $150\\%$ *greater than* $20,$ we apply a new percentage of  \n\n$$\n100\\% + 150\\% = 250\\%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting our percentage to a decimal:  \n\n$$\n250\\% = \\dfrac{250}{100} = 2.5\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $150\\%$ greater than $20,$ we multiply $20$ by $2.5{:}$  \n\n$$\n2.5 \\cdot 20 = 50\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x = {50}.$",
